    "field": "Coupled climate-carbon cycle modeling",
    "problem": "The strength of the feedback between the carbon cycle and climate is uncertain, as it is unclear how this feedback, which can amplify warming, is affected by the climate's underlying sensitivity to increased atmospheric CO2\u2014a major uncertainty in climate projections.",
    "method": "The paper investigates the sensitivity of carbon cycle feedbacks by using a coupled climate-carbon model (INCCA) to simulate terrestrial and ocean carbon uptake under the SRES A2 emissions scenario, while artificially imposing different climate sensitivities to produce global warming scenarios ranging from 0 to 8 K.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the sensitivity of carbon cycle-climate feedback to different levels of climate sensitivity, using a coupled model to simulate global warming scenarios ranging from 0 to 8 K by the year 2100 for the SRES A2 emissions scenario.",
